title: Quantity type rejects valid n/u SI suffixes (100n dies on 30 fields)
updated: 2026-08-27T18:48:26Z
---

lib/IO/K8s/Types.pm:16 -- the suffix class in the Quantity regex is
[mkMGTPE]; upstream apimachinery (suffix.go) also allows n (nano) and
u (micro) as decimal SI suffixes.

Repro (measured): Quantity->check("100n") is rejected;
IO::K8s::Api::Core::V1::EmptyDirVolumeSource->new(sizeLimit => "100n")
dies with a type constraint error. Counter-check: 100m, 1Ki, 2e3 pass.

Impact: inflating real cluster data fails -- metrics-server reports CPU
as e.g. 100n, autoscaling/v2 MetricTarget/MetricValueStatus averageValue
carries such values. Affects the 30 fields typed Quantity; fields typed
{ Str => 1 } (e.g. ResourceRequirements requests/limits) are NOT affected.

Fix sketch: widen the suffix class to [numkMGTPE]. Regression tests for
100n/500u accept plus the existing matrix staying green.

Found in the 2026-08-18 core-module review (repro verified).
Lane: io-k8s-worker, then io-k8s-test-writer.

Fixed: suffix class widened to [numkMGTPE], matching the decimal table in upstream suffix.go. Verified differentially against a Perl port of parseQuantityString over 2743 strings. Mantissa-less forms (Ki, m, .) stay rejected on purpose although upstream parses them as 0. Tests: t/21_quantity_time.t.
